# L §5.14.3 How a settlement leg counts: "A version that turns a leg round, a place its `from` on one side and its `to`
# on the other, gives settlement legs no sign: they are refused (RUN-RECORD), and only a waiver settles it"; L §8.4
# `settlement <m> of <adjustment>: the leg is turned round`. turn swaps t[2026-03]'s places (konto -> konto2 becomes
# konto2 -> konto); bank[r1] settling it is refused, and konto's balance with it (b).
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source act "act"
source bank_export "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place konto2: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int
input src: key accounts
input dst: key accounts
input bank: observed
def s_[m in months]: key accounts = src at start_of(m)
def d_[m in months]: key accounts = dst at start_of(m)

move t[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from s_[m] to d_[m] amount amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "umowa"
  dom = 10 "umowa"
  src = konto "umowa"
  dst = konto2 "umowa"
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version turn
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace src = konto2 "aneks"
  replace dst = konto "aneks"

version settle
  cite bank_export
  governs 2026-05
  known 2026-05-20
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-05-15, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto2 to konto amount 100.00 PLN, fulfils: adjustments[t[2026-03].cash, turn]) "line 1"

ask b: bal(konto, 2026-05-31)
=== expect
b: refused: RUN-RECORD settlement bank[r1] of adjustments[t[2026-03].cash, turn]: the leg is turned round
  cut 2026-10-20
